00:00:00.690 --> 00:00:04.710
Rhiannon: If a child or young person is
experiencing anxiety, there are things

00:00:04.710 --> 00:00:06.470
that parents and carers can do to help.

00:00:06.960 --> 00:00:10.219
Firstly, it's important to talk
to their child about their stress,

00:00:10.460 --> 00:00:14.450
anxiety or worries and reassure them,
that their feelings are understood

00:00:14.500 --> 00:00:16.439
and try to help them find solutions.

00:00:17.379 --> 00:00:21.279
Leah: If the child is old enough, it
may help to explain what anxiety is and

00:00:21.280 --> 00:00:23.050
the physical effects it has on the body.

00:00:23.660 --> 00:00:27.160
It’s worthwhile trying to get a
child to recognise signs of anxiety

00:00:27.179 --> 00:00:30.980
in themselves and encourage them to
learn to try to manage their anxiety

00:00:31.119 --> 00:00:32.639
and ask for help when they need it.

00:00:33.740 --> 00:00:38.290
Children of all ages find routines
reassuring, so sticking to regular

00:00:38.290 --> 00:00:42.330
daily routines where possible can help
them to keep on top of their anxiety.

00:00:42.640 --> 00:00:46.130
Rhiannon: If a child is worried about
something in particular, it’s best to

00:00:46.130 --> 00:00:50.469
find solutions or plans to help them feel
that they can get through it, so that

00:00:50.469 --> 00:00:54.469
their anxiety will not overwhelm them
and stop them doing things in the future.

00:00:55.439 --> 00:00:58.810
Leah: If a child is anxious because
of distressing events, such as a

00:00:58.900 --> 00:01:02.949
bereavement or family breakup, a parent
could look for books or films that

00:01:02.950 --> 00:01:06.819
might help them in understanding their
feelings and help to discuss things

00:01:06.830 --> 00:01:08.560
that happen and issues that arise.

00:01:09.410 --> 00:01:13.070
Rhiannon: If a change is due to happen,
such as a house move, a child can be

00:01:13.070 --> 00:01:16.950
prepared for the changes by talking
to them about what is going to happen

00:01:17.140 --> 00:01:21.360
and looking at all the positives such
as choosing their decor, finding new

00:01:21.360 --> 00:01:25.650
places to go, and trying to visit the
area and getting to know it in advance.

00:01:26.139 --> 00:01:29.770
Leah: Distraction can be helpful for young
children, for example, if they are anxious

00:01:29.770 --> 00:01:33.940
about something or going somewhere keep
them entertained on the way there, or give

00:01:33.940 --> 00:01:35.500
them something new to get involved in.

